<div class="prose">

  <h2>What your staff receive</h2>
  <p>One email every Monday morning for each specialty they choose. It summarises every new paper published that week in the top five journals in that field. Each summary links to the original paper.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>31 medical specialties.</strong> Each person chooses their own, and can choose more than one. The journals for each are listed on our <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>A CPD log.</strong> Every article has a "Log as CPD" button. Reading is recorded with a reflection in the reader's own words, and exports for appraisal or revalidation.</li>
    <li><strong>Nothing to visit.</strong> The Brief arrives in the inbox. Nobody has to remember to look for it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The summaries are generated automatically from each paper's abstract. Our <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> sets out how that works and where its limits are.</p>

  <h2>How a licence works</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><strong>You tell us about your organisation.</strong> Roughly how many staff you have, and the email addresses they use. We reply with a price and send one annual invoice.</li>
    <li><strong>We build a sign-up page for you.</strong> It accepts only your organisation's email addresses, so it does not matter if the link is passed on.</li>
    <li><strong>Staff sign up themselves.</strong> They give their name and work email and choose their specialties. There is no payment step.</li>
    <li><strong>We check each sign-up and send a welcome email.</strong> From then on the Brief arrives every Monday.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>There is no charge per person and no charge for extra specialties. There is nothing for your team to administer.</p>

  <h2>On your intranet or learning platform</h2>
  <p>The Brief needs one small entry: a short description, a sample issue and the sign-up link. We supply the wording and the logo. Nothing on the page needs updating from week to week.</p>
  <p>We do not post the Brief itself there. Staff choose their own specialties, so there is no single edition to post. And a weekly digest works because it arrives.</p>

  <h2>If you run a library or a journal club</h2>
  <p>Many education teams and librarians already pick out papers by hand, for a current-awareness bulletin or a journal club. The Brief gives you each week's new papers from five journals, already summarised, to choose from.</p>

  <h2>Before you launch</h2>
  <p>Hospice and hospital mail systems often filter email from a sender they have not seen before. We send each person their own copy, so a filter can stop every one of them.</p>
  <p>Before launch we ask your IT team to allow our sending address, and we test it with you. It is a small job, and it decides whether your staff see the Brief at all.</p>

  <h2>Your staff's data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We collect each person's name, work email address and choice of specialties</li>
    <li>We can tell you how many of your staff have signed up. We do not tell you who, or which specialties anyone chose</li>
    <li>We delete a person's sign-up details within 30 days of them unsubscribing or the licence ending</li>
    <li>CPD records are visible only to the person who wrote them</li>
    <li>No patient information is involved at any point</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The detail is in our <a href="/privacy.html">privacy policy</a>. We can send a fuller note on data handling for your information governance lead.</p>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Who pays for the Brief</strong>
    Its readers, and nobody else. We carry no advertising and no sponsored content, and we take no payment from pharmaceutical companies or journal publishers.
  </div>

  <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
  <p>The Monday Clinical Brief is built and run by Dr Tim Hamilton, a Consultant in Palliative Medicine in NHS Wales. More about him, and about how we produce and check what we publish, is on the <a href="/about/">about page</a>.</p>

  <div class="ask">
    <h2>Ask about a licence</h2>
    <p>Tell us what kind of organisation you are and roughly how many staff you have. We will reply with a price and a sample issue for your specialty.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="mailto:info@mondayclinicalbrief.co.uk?subject=Organisation%20licence">Email info@mondayclinicalbrief.co.uk</a>
    <p class="small">Subscribing for yourself? <a href="/#subscribe">Start a free trial</a>.</p>
  </div>

